Can you get owner and schema name before we go further? Give me all the scripts you need to dump packages, stored proc and functions

Building scripts to discover and dump database schema objects.

Run these in order. Step 1 finds the owner and schema, and the dump script in step 2 then uses what you find.

Step 1: Find the schema and package names

Run each statement separately with Ctrl+Enter.

sql
-- 1a. Who am I connected as?
SELECT USER AS login_user,
       SYS_CONTEXT('USERENV','CURRENT_SCHEMA') AS current_schema,
       SYS_CONTEXT('USERENV','DB_NAME')        AS db_name
FROM   dual;

-- 1b. Which schema owns CES_ARCHIVE? (this gives the exact owner name)
SELECT owner, object_name, object_type, status
FROM   all_objects
WHERE  object_name = 'CES_ARCHIVE';

-- 1c. Which schemas have code, and how much of each kind?
SELECT owner, object_type, COUNT(*) AS cnt
FROM   all_objects
WHERE  object_type IN ('PACKAGE','PACKAGE BODY','PROCEDURE','FUNCTION')
AND    owner NOT IN ('SYS','SYSTEM','XDB','MDSYS','CTXSYS','ORDSYS','OUTLN','DBSNMP',
                     'APEX_030200','APEX_040200','APPQOSSYS','WMSYS','ORDDATA','LBACSYS')
GROUP  BY owner, object_type
ORDER  BY owner, object_type;

-- 1d. List the names in the schema you picked (change MYSCHEMA)
SELECT object_type, object_name, status
FROM   all_objects
WHERE  owner = 'MYSCHEMA'
AND    object_type IN ('PACKAGE BODY','PROCEDURE','FUNCTION')
ORDER  BY object_type, object_name;

Step 2: Dump the code

This is one script for all three kinds of code. It writes a separate text file for each, and sets p_pkg to % to dump every package body at once.

sql
-- Run with Run Script (F5). Edit the three DEFINE lines.
DEFINE p_owner  = 'MYSCHEMA'
DEFINE p_pkg    = 'CES_ARCHIVE'    -- or % for all package bodies
DEFINE p_folder = 'C:/temp'        -- must already exist

SET ECHO OFF FEEDBACK OFF HEADING OFF VERIFY OFF PAGESIZE 0
SET LINESIZE 4000 LONG 1000000 TRIMSPOOL ON SQLBLANKLINES ON TERMOUT ON

SPOOL &p_folder./package_bodies.sql
SELECT src FROM (
  SELECT name, line ord,
         CASE WHEN line = 1 THEN 'CREATE OR REPLACE ' END || RTRIM(text, CHR(10)||CHR(13)) src
  FROM   all_source
  WHERE  owner = UPPER('&p_owner') AND type = 'PACKAGE BODY' AND name LIKE UPPER('&p_pkg')
  UNION ALL
  SELECT name, MAX(line)+1, '/' || CHR(10)
  FROM   all_source
  WHERE  owner = UPPER('&p_owner') AND type = 'PACKAGE BODY' AND name LIKE UPPER('&p_pkg')
  GROUP  BY name
) ORDER BY name, ord;
SPOOL OFF

SPOOL &p_folder./procedures.sql
SELECT src FROM (
  SELECT name, line ord,
         CASE WHEN line = 1 THEN 'CREATE OR REPLACE ' END || RTRIM(text, CHR(10)||CHR(13)) src
  FROM   all_source WHERE owner = UPPER('&p_owner') AND type = 'PROCEDURE'
  UNION ALL
  SELECT name, MAX(line)+1, '/' || CHR(10)
  FROM   all_source WHERE owner = UPPER('&p_owner') AND type = 'PROCEDURE' GROUP BY name
) ORDER BY name, ord;
SPOOL OFF

SPOOL &p_folder./functions.sql
SELECT src FROM (
  SELECT name, line ord,
         CASE WHEN line = 1 THEN 'CREATE OR REPLACE ' END || RTRIM(text, CHR(10)||CHR(13)) src
  FROM   all_source WHERE owner = UPPER('&p_owner') AND type = 'FUNCTION'
  UNION ALL
  SELECT name, MAX(line)+1, '/' || CHR(10)
  FROM   all_source WHERE owner = UPPER('&p_owner') AND type = 'FUNCTION' GROUP BY name
) ORDER BY name, ord;
SPOOL OFF

PROMPT Done. Files written to &p_folder.
